{"title":"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 26","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb1e7567daf504db9ed16914050e267f81e4902c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(arc((0,-1),2,30,150),dashed+linewidth(.75)); draw((-1.7,0)--(0,0)--(1.7,0),dot); draw((0,0)--(0,.98),dot); MP(&quot;A&quot;,(-1.7,0),W);MP(&quot;B&quot;,(1.7,0),E);MP(&quot;M&quot;,(0,0),S);MP(&quot;C&quot;,(0,1),N); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"102\" />\n</p><p>A parabolic arch has a height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> inches and a span of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> inches. The height, in inches, of the arch at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inches from the center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/8/5c8137022ea2dcd176514ed2c43013cb11d36a5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } 1\\quad \\text{(B) } 15\\quad \\text{(C) } 15\\tfrac{1}{3}\\quad \\text{(D) } 15\\tfrac{1}{2}\\quad \\text{(E) } 15\\tfrac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"331\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because the arch has a height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> inches, an equation that models the arch is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/6/f5637f59b7c310728ff38194305b1bc3c30cb43b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = ax^2 + 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the horizontal distance from the center and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is the height.  The arch has a span of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> inches, so the arch meets the ground <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> inches from the center.  That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/e/61eedae4cbb162b9c1b53cf4c7b15bab950cf7cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 = 400a + 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd8a7d7dde93e6eebeba5a655e48c90c1125025e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = -\\frac{1}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"68\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the equation that models height based on distance from the center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f060b83464e79b25a9e321c83c9211dc38e41e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -\\frac{1}{25}x^2 + 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"127\" height=\"37\" />, so the height of the arch <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inches from the center is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/c/2aced78196bcd8b229451baa5d06cc5086d43ca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{25} \\cdot 5^2 + 16 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"195\" height=\"37\" /> inches.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME\" title=\"1969 AHSME\">1969 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1969 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1969\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"5